# ============================================================================
#  .gitignore for date-fruit-project
# ============================================================================
#  The trained model file is NOT in Git. At 322.6 MiB it exceeds GitHub's hard
#  100 MiB per-file push limit, so it is distributed by download instead.
#    model/date_fruit_model.keras   -> IGNORED (download it separately)
#    model/classes.json             -> tracked (94 bytes, and it is the single
#                                      source of truth for the class order)
#  See "A note on the model file and Git" in README.md for the download link.
#  Also intentionally tracked: README.md, all source code, Alembic migrations,
#  the test_images/ folder, and both .env.example files (they contain
#  placeholders, never real secrets).
# ============================================================================

# --- The trained model -----------------------------------------------------
# Ignored by filename, not by folder, so model/classes.json stays tracked.
model/date_fruit_model.keras
*.keras

# --- Secrets: never commit a real .env -------------------------------------
# A bare pattern like ".env" matches at every directory level, so this also
# covers backend/.env and frontend/.env. ".env.example" does NOT match these
# patterns, so the example files stay tracked.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.claude/
claude/
# --- Node / React ----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Uploaded listing images -----------------------------------------------
# Photographs published by users belong to whoever is running the application,
# not to the repository. The folder itself must still exist in a fresh clone,
# though, or the first publish would fail - and Git cannot store an empty
# folder. So the contents are ignored and the .gitkeep placeholder is kept, via
# the "!" pattern which un-ignores a single file.
backend/uploads/listings/*
!backend/uploads/listings/.gitkeep

# --- Editors / IDEs --------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- Operating system junk -------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Logs & temporary files ------------------------------------------------
*.log
tmp/
temp/
